486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 302 0 R
/E (Cloud Forensics Automation for Retail Breaches is a comprehensive cybersecurity and digital forensics platform developed to detect unauthorized modifications, suspicious activities, and integrity violations within retail transaction systems. Designed as an academic cybersecurity project, the platform integrates a simulated retail management application with an automated forensic monitoring engine to demonstrate practical security monitoring and incident detection in modern retail environments.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 302 0 R
/E (The system is developed using Python and Streamlit and operates on a lightweight file- based architecture that continuously monitors transaction logs, activity records, and critical retail data stored within the monitored environment. Instead of treating security as a secondary component, the project embeds forensic analysis directly into the operational workflow by implementing SHA-256 cryptographic hashing for integrity verification and automated tampering detection mechanisms. The platform continuously compares file hashes to identify unauthorized modifications and immediately flags altered files as potential security threats.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 302 0 R
/E (To simulate real-world retail breach scenarios, the system includes a live retail transaction simulator where sales records, inventory updates, and activity logs are dynamically generated. A forensic dashboard then performs automated scans on these files, extracts metadata, analyzes timestamps, and identifies suspicious activities such as malicious entries or unauthorized data manipulation. The platform also maintains audit logs and provides downloadable forensic reports in CSV format to preserve the chain of custody during investigations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 302 0 R
/E (The application features an interactive Streamlit-based Security Operations Center \(SOC\) dashboard that visualizes system status, suspicious files, tampered records, and overall file integrity in real time. Additional functionalities include simulated cyberattack injection, automated report generation, and role-based monitoring workflows that help demonstrate incident response procedures in retail systems. Ultimately, Cloud Forensics Automation for Retail Breaches serves as a secure, practical, and user-friendly demonstration of how digital forensic techniques, file integrity monitoring, and automated threat detection can be integrated into retail infrastructures to improve cybersecurity resilience and support breach investigations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 302 0 R
/T (ABSTRACT )
/E (ABSTRACT )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
