/P 305 0 R
/E (The system is designed to continuously monitor retail transaction files, activity logs, inventory records, and operational data stored within monitored directories. By using SHA-256 cryptographic hashing, the platform verifies file integrity and identifies any unauthorized modifications performed on critical retail data. Whenever file tampering occurs, the system automatically flags the affected files and displays alerts through a centralized forensic monitoring dashboard.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 305 0 R
/E (Another important aim of the project is to demonstrate how digital forensic techniques can be automated for real-time cybersecurity monitoring. The platform performs continuous file analysis, metadata extraction, integrity verification, suspicious activity detection, and forensic report generation without requiring manual investigation for every operation. This helps improve the efficiency of identifying cyber threats and preserving digital evidence.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
