1031 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 317 0 R
/E (Modern retail systems continuously generate large amounts of digital information such as transaction records, customer billing details, inventory data, activity logs, and operational files. These files contain sensitive information that must be protected against unauthorized access, tampering, and cyber threats. However, many traditional retail systems focus mainly on operational efficiency and billing management while providing limited support for forensic monitoring and integrity verification.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1032 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 317 0 R
/E (One of the major problems in existing retail environments is the lack of automated cybersecurity monitoring systems capable of detecting unauthorized modifications in real time. If attackers modify transaction records, inject malicious entries, delete important logs, or manipulate billing information, the organization may not immediately detect the attack. Delayed detection increases the difficulty of forensic investigation and creates major risks for retail infrastructures.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [7]
>>
