<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (designed to overcome the limitations and security weaknesses present in traditional retail systems. The system integrates digital forensic monitoring, file integrity verification, tampering detection, real-time dashboard visualization, and forensic report generation into a single secure platform. The main objective of the proposed system is to automatically identify unauthorized modifications and suspicious activities within retail transaction environments.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (The proposed system combines a simulated retail management application with an automated forensic monitoring engine. The retail application continuously)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (generates transaction records, billing information, inventory updates, and activity logs that are stored inside monitored directories. The forensic engine continuously scans these files, analyzes their metadata, generates SHA-256 hash values, and compares them with previously stored values to verify file integrity.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (Whenever a file is modified without authorization, the system immediately detects the integrity violation through hash mismatch analysis. The affected files are automatically marked as tampered, and alerts are displayed through the forensic dashboard. This enables investigators and administrators to quickly identify suspicious modifications and respond to cybersecurity incidents effectively.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (The proposed system introduces real-time forensic monitoring capabilities that are absent in traditional retail systems. Instead of relying on manual investigation processes, the platform automates file analysis, integrity verification, threat detection, activity logging, and forensic report generation. This improves investigation speed, enhances cybersecurity visibility, and reduces operational)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
